{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfRiaicSsMyXmADoB6ffg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GF2qhCixSNqQ7LXjmuNxgi","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/jim/src/apps/odd_glc/.ai-workspace/comments/codex/20260924_HELLO_PROJECT_BASELINE/full-native-remaining-01/js-sdlc-bootstrap/subject-js-sdlc-bootstrap/design/test-design.md","content":"# Test Design\n\nEvidence source: package.json and src/hello.mjs\n\npackage.json declares \"private\": true and \"type\": \"module\". src/hello.mjs\nexports the named, synchronous function helloWorld(), which returns exactly\n\"Hello, world!\".\n\n## Component validation obligation\n\ntest/component/hello.test.mjs imports helloWorld from src/hello.mjs and\nasserts by strict equality that the return value of helloWorld() is exactly\n\"Hello, world!\".\n\n## UAT validation obligation\n\ntest/uat/hello.uat.test.mjs validates the user-visible greeting contract\nthrough the same exported function. The user is a JavaScript consumer that\nimports helloWorld from src/hello.mjs and calls it; the greeting it receives\nmust be exactly \"Hello, world!\", asserted by strict equality.\n\n## Constraints on both tests\n\nBoth tests use node:test and node:assert/strict. Each file declares exactly\none test through test(). Test names are prefixed 'component:' and 'uat:'.\nNeither test uses skip, todo, only, describe or it. Neither test uses stdout,\na CLI or any other surface; both observe only the return value of the same\nexported function.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2102,"cache_read_input_tokens":519484,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2102},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2c77afa6-0d37-4ec9-be28-84c396f5738c","uuid":"7bc56cc7-e268-462d-9214-096a769c1ac7","timestamp":"2026-09-26T08:15:03.794Z","request_id":"req_011CfRiai4xougMBGnDihmEh","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01GF2qhCixSNqQ7LXjmuNxgi":{"file_path":"/Users/jim/src/apps/odd_glc/.ai-workspace/comments/codex/20260924_HELLO_PROJECT_BASELINE/full-native-remaining-01/js-sdlc-bootstrap/subject-js-sdlc-bootstrap/design/test-design.md","content":"# Test Design\n\nEvidence source: package.json and src/hello.mjs\n\npackage.json declares \"private\": true and \"type\": \"module\". src/hello.mjs\nexports the named, synchronous function helloWorld(), which returns exactly\n\"Hello, world!\".\n\n## Component validation obligation\n\ntest/component/hello.test.mjs imports helloWorld from src/hello.mjs and\nasserts by strict equality that the return value of helloWorld() is exactly\n\"Hello, world!\".\n\n## UAT validation obligation\n\ntest/uat/hello.uat.test.mjs validates the user-visible greeting contract\nthrough the same exported function. The user is a JavaScript consumer that\nimports helloWorld from src/hello.mjs and calls it; the greeting it receives\nmust be exactly \"Hello, world!\", asserted by strict equality.\n\n## Constraints on both tests\n\nBoth tests use node:test and node:assert/strict. Each file declares exactly\none test through test(). Test names are prefixed 'component:' and 'uat:'.\nNeither test uses skip, todo, only, describe or it. Neither test uses stdout,\na CLI or any other surface; both observe only the return value of the same\nexported function.\n"}}}
